Licence and attribution for the word data
=========================================

The files in this directory — concepts.json and core_concepts.tsv — are
licensed under the

    Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International Licence
    (CC BY-SA 4.0)  ·  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

This is NOT the MIT licence that covers the rest of the repository. concepts.json
is built from Creative Commons BY-SA dictionaries, so it is a derivative work and
must stay under a compatible share-alike licence. If you redistribute it, modified
or not, you must keep this licence, keep the attributions below, and release your
changes under CC BY-SA 4.0.

core_concepts.tsv is written by hand by this project's author and is offered under
the same licence so that the two files can be used together without confusion.


Sources
-------

Spanish — FreeDict eng-spa
    https://freedict.org · derived from the English Wiktionary
    Licence: CC BY-SA 3.0, relicensed here to 4.0 as that licence permits.

Mandarin Chinese — CC-CEDICT
    https://www.mdbg.net/chinese/dictionary?page=cc-cedict
    Published by MDBG. Referenced works: CEDICT, Copyright (C) 1997, 1998
    Paul Andrew Denisowski.
    Licence: CC BY-SA 4.0.

Vietnamese — Vietnamese Wiktionary, English section, via kaikki.org
    https://kaikki.org/viwiktionary/ · extracted by wiktextract from
    https://vi.wiktionary.org
    Licence: CC BY-SA 4.0 (Wiktionary text, also available under the GFDL).

Word ordering — hermitdave/FrequencyWords
    https://github.com/hermitdave/FrequencyWords
    Frequency lists built from the OpenSubtitles corpus.
    Licence: MIT, Copyright (c) 2016 Hermit Dave.

Pinyin, part-of-speech tags and the choice of which word represents each
concept are produced by build_concepts.py in this repository.


If you only want the code
-------------------------

Delete data/concepts.json and run `python3 build_concepts.py` to regenerate it
from the sources yourself. The MIT licence then covers everything you hold,
and the rebuilt file carries the same obligations as above.
